## Controller rulings

1. Do not create or expand tests until the optimizer goal completes end to end. The user's explicit instruction overrides this plan's test-file additions. Each implementation task must instead use existing focused tests, compile/lint checks, and direct deterministic smoke evidence appropriate to the changed source. Cost if wrong: early regression localization is weaker, so reviews must scrutinize boundary behavior closely.
2. Stop this detailed plan after Task 5 and resume Tasks 6–7 only after the roadmap's strategy, universe, artifact graph, hidden-panel, learning, and search phases provide their declared inputs. Cost if wrong: additional coordination and context switching; benefit: no placeholder contracts or duplicated evidence paths.
3. V5 remains opt-in. Legacy V2–V4 execution must remain reproducible, and baseline/candidate comparisons must use the same execution and friction identities.
4. No OpenRouter/provider calls, qualification, full replay, Docker execution, pushing, or merging are authorized by this phase.

